  "_doc": "Documents pre-existing review-blocker DEBT in committed .maxpat files so tests/test_integration_patches.py::test_review_patch_no_blockers can exempt ONLY these specific findings. Committed patches are frozen (never edited to satisfy critics -- regression constraint). Exemptions are per-patch AND per-blocker-signature: a new patch (path not listed here) or a new blocker (signature not explicitly listed for its patch) is NEVER exempted and still fails. Fan-out entries (CLAUDE.md Rule #4 fan-out-without-trigger) match on (source_id, outlet); Bach-llll entries (send/receive routing-bridge false positives -- a receive object's output llll-ness is statically unknowable) match on (source_id, inlet, sorted destinations). source/destinations names are kept for human auditability. This is a TEST-only exemption; critic behavior at generation time is unchanged. MAINTENANCE: because a new patch is never auto-exempted, this file must be extended whenever a patch lands with pre-existing blocker debt -- otherwise test_review_patch_no_blockers accrues permanent failures and stops functioning as a gate. The original 14 entries were committed 85b8f92 on 2026-07-02 and went stale as later patches landed; quick-260921-gut added 6 more (looper, reverse-delay, reverse-delay-mono, simple-fm, stereo-feedback-delay, terrain-osc-test) for patches saved between 2026-08-19 and 2026-09-21. Each entry added from that task onward carries a `reason` field recording why that specific blocker is exempt; `_entry_key()` ignores the field, so it is documentation that cannot drift away from the exemption it justifies.",
